<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumatra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sumatra is a large island in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, lying along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a>. It was the home of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palembang">Palembang</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> profiles discuss later control of the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sumatra.jpg" alt="Sumatra" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sadalmelik · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sumatra_Topography.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
